SUMMARY:Sleepy Gap loop
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/DKGBZoKru
 XHUncka7](https://maps.app.goo.gl/DKGBZoKruXHUncka7)\n\napprox 4 miles\, 8
 00 feet of elevation gain\n\nthis is a fun and largely shaded shorter loop
  starting at the Sleepy Gap Overlook\, which is on the right going south o
 n the BRP from the Arboretum after passing thru the Grassy Knob tunnel. I'
 m pretty sure the location pin is accurate but not 100%\n\nfrom Sleepy Gap
  we take the MST to Chestnut Cove\, then Chestnut Cove trail down to South
  Ridge Road\, then ascend the Sleepy Gap trail back to the overlook.\n\nno
 te the change to 10 a.m. starting time\n\npace of 2.0 - 2.5 mph\n\nwell be
 haved dogs are welcome to attend\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appr
 opriate\, trekking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a brea
 k mid-hike. and plenty of water\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, show 
 up or change your status. 2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape t
 o complete the event. 3) show consideration toward all atendees. I hike fo
 r stress reduction and want to keep it that way as much as possible\n\n**L
 EGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibl
 y\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsib
 le for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\,
  physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risk
 s to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hikin
 g Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for 
 this event\, participant understands and agrees
